  "title": "DGTR Investigates and Proposes Anti-Dumping Duties on Rubber Gloves",
  "summary": "The DGTR initiated an investigation into imported rubber gloves from Thailand and Malaysia, alleging dumping of goods into Indian markets. The commission recommended imposing up to $565 per one lakh pieces of anti-dumping duty to protect domestic manufacturers, with a final decision expected by the finance ministry.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The DGTR investigated imports of medical examination rubber gloves from Thailand and Malaysia",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The commission recommended a duty ranging between USD 442 and USD 565",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The duty will protect domestic manufacturers from cheap imports from the source countries",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
