      "title": "DGTR proposes anti-dumping duty of up to $565 on rubber glove imports",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/industry/news/dgtr-proposes-anti-dumping-duty-of-up-to-565-on-rubber-glove-imports-126110900501_1.html",
      "description": "The commerce ministry's investigation arm, DGTR, has recommended imposing up to USD 565 per one lakh pieces anti-dumping duty on imports of medical examination rubber gloves imported from Thailand and Malaysia for five years, according to a notification.\nThe duty will help guard domestic manufacturers of the product from cheap imports from these two countries.\nThe Directorate General of Trade Remedies (DGTR) recommended the duty after probing the impact of alleged dumping of these goods into Indian markets by makers in Thailand and Malaysia.\n\"The authority considers it necessary and recommends the imposition of definitive anti-dumping duty on imports of the subject goods originating in or exported from the subject countries,\" the DGTR has said in a notification.\nThe recommended duty ranges between USD 442 per one lakh pieces and USD 565 per one lakh pieces, it said.\nThe final decision to impose the duty will be taken by the finance ministry.\nIn its final findings, the DGTR conclu",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-09T08:42:12"
    }
